## Complexity
Each iteration divides n by 10, reducing the number of digits by one. A number with d digits requires d - 1 iterations, so the time complexity is O(log10(n)).

**Space Complexity:**
Only the input variable and one counter are used, with no data structure depending on input size. The auxiliary space complexity is O(1).

